                <pb facs="1099" n="949" sameAs="frus:frus1907p2/pg949"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File 3714/1.</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Persian Minister to the
                            Secretary of State.</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Translation.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation of Persia</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1907-01-09"><hi rendition="#italic">January 9,
                        1907</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>Mr. <hi rendition="#small-caps">Minister</hi>: I fulfill a very painful duty in
                    communicating to your excellency the sorrowful calamity that has stricken the
                    Persian nation in the decease of its beloved and regretted sovereign
                    Mozaffer-ed-Dine Shah.</p>
                <p>Please accept, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Morteza.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
